in October 2000 the president of Iraq's  Saddam Hussein announced they would no  longer be selling oil in U.S dollars  only in Euros so when Hussein decided to  start selling oil in Euros instead of  dollars the US wasn't too happy by  February 2003 he has sold over 3 billion  barrels of oil for 26 billion euros a  month later the U.S invaded Iraq in an  operation ironically called operation  Iraqi Freedom they overthrew Saddam and  by June just four months later the  country was back to selling oil in  dollars years later a number of U.S  officials started to let the truth seep  out former head of U.S operations in  Iraq General John abbazade said of  course it's about oil we can't really  deny that former fed chairman Alan  Greenspan wrote in his Memoir that quote  I'm certain that is politically  inconvenient to acknowledge what  everyone knows the Iraq war is largely  about oil End quotes and former Defense  secretary Chuck Hagel said the same in  2007. quote people say we're not  fighting for oil of course we are End  quotes click the link in the pin comment  to learn more
 

